.TH "cbor::schema::at_path" "3" "2026-11-01" "mbedded\-cbor 0.9.0" "mbedded\-cbor"
.SH NAME
cbor::schema::at_path \- reads one number, \(gabool\(ga or enum with no accessor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IP
.EX
#include \f[B]<cbor/cbor.hpp>\f[R]
.EE
.IP
.EX
\f[B]template\f[R] <fixed_string Path, std::convertible_to<std::size_t>... Index>
    \f[B]requires\f[R](has_describe_members<std::remove_cv_t<T>> && tags_registered<T>() && Path.view().starts_with(\(aq$\(aq) &&
             reflection::path_valid<T, Path, 1>() && \f[B]sizeof\f[R]...(Index) == reflection::index_arguments<Path>() &&
             value_holds_no_view<\f[B]typename\f[R] \f[B]decltype\f[R](reflection::path_result<T, T, Path, 1>())::type>)
static \f[B]auto\f[R] at_path(std::string_view const encoded, Index const... indexes);
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
Member of cbor::schema<T>.
.PP
Reads one value at \f[CR]Path\f[R] and returns a
\f[CR]std::expected\f[R] of it.
It makes the checks of path and of an accessor in one call and keeps
nothing.
It exists only for a value that holds no view into the bytes: a number,
a \f[CR]bool\f[R], an enum, or a \f[CR]std::optional\f[R] of one.
.PP
A path starts with \f[CR]$\f[R], names a member with \f[CR].name\f[R]
and an element with \f[CR][n]\f[R].
\f[CR][]\f[R] takes its index from the next argument.
On an array or a vector of \f[CR]std::uint8_t\f[R] or
\f[CR]std::byte\f[R], \f[CR][n]\f[R] reads one byte.
A text, a list or a struct needs an accessor.
.SH ERRORS
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]too_little_data\f[R], \f[CR]incorrect_type\f[R]: as path.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]index_out_of_bounds\f[R]: an index past the end of a list.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]unpopulated_table_index\f[R], \f[CR]syntax_error\f[R]: a broken
reference.
.IP \(bu 2
A member that \f[CR]T\f[R] does not have, a wrong count of indexes, or a
path to a text does not compile.
.SH NOTES
O(q + p): q the size of the table prefix, p the count of steps of the
path.
No allocation.
.SH EXAMPLES
.IP
.EX
\f[I]// bytes: from schema<car>::encode(car{\(dqVolvo\(dq, 5, {{17, 2.5f}, {18, 2.25f}}, {1.0, 2.0, 3.0}})\f[R]
cbor::schema<car>::at_path<\(dq$.seats\(dq>(bytes);                    \f[I]// 5\f[R]
cbor::schema<car>::at_path<\(dq$.tires[1].diameter\(dq>(bytes);        \f[I]// 18\f[R]
cbor::schema<car>::at_path<\(dq$.tires[].diameter\(dq>(bytes, 5uz);    \f[I]// error::index_out_of_bounds\f[R]
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
